# Docker build context — only what the trafico-web image needs.
# Without this, 225 GB of tile build artifacts under /opt/trafico/tiles/build/
# were being tar'd into every build, breaking COPY with "read/write on closed pipe".

# Build artifacts from Planetiler / OSRM / tippecanoe (on compute only).
# Match at ANY depth — compute has /opt/trafico/tiles/tiles/*.pmtiles (2 levels),
# /opt/trafico/tiles/build/*.osm.pbf (mixed), etc. A previous single-level
# pattern missed the 75 GB planet pmtiles and blew up `docker build`.
tiles/
services/tiles/build/

# OSRM routing graphs — 27 GB of car/bike/foot data under /opt/trafico/osrm on
# compute, consumed by the separate trafico-osrm-* containers, never by the web
# image. The comment above mentions OSRM but the pattern only ever covered
# tiles/, so this was still being tar'd into every build: measured 2026-08-16 at
# a 28.31 GB build context, 93 s just to transfer plus 118 s on COPY, turning a
# ~12 min deploy into over an hour and churning enough layers to contribute to a
# HostDiskWarning. No source file references this path.
osrm/

# Dependencies — installed inside the image
node_modules/
packages/*/node_modules/
.pnp.*

# Next.js output — rebuilt inside the image
.next/
out/

# Environment + secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Git
.git/
.gitignore

# CI / editor / OS
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Test + coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright-mcp/

# Blitz / Claude session state
.blitz/
.claude/
.claude-session
.claude-profiles/

# Docs that don't ship in the image
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Backup / scratch files
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.sql.gz
nav-snapshot.md
